Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

* Align blazor-wasm-servicedefaults template with Aspire client defaults

Fixes #67032: the WASM app threw CircularDependencyException
(ILoggerFactory) on startup when OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT was not
configured, because the OTel logger provider activates
OtlpExporterOptions while the LoggerFactory is being constructed and our
IPostConfigureOptions resolved ILoggerFactory from the same container.

- Skip OpenTelemetry wiring entirely when OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
  is empty. This is the contract Aspire's BlazorHosted /
  BlazorStandalone ClientServiceDefaults already follow.
- Resolve the OTLP path against HostEnvironment.BaseAddress and set
  per-signal endpoints (v1/logs, v1/metrics, v1/traces) so telemetry
  flows through the same origin as the WASM page.
- Use a fixed serviceInstanceId so all browser tabs report as a single
  instance in the dashboard.
- Drop the redundant AddComponentsMetrics / AddComponentsTracing calls;
  WebAssemblyHostBuilder registers them automatically on net11+ when
  Meter.IsSupported is true (now the default).
- console.warn on /_blazor/_configuration fetch failures in the
  standalone JS initializer so the no-gateway case is diagnosable.
- Add Run-BlazorWasmServiceDefaults-Locally.ps1 to iterate on the
  template content the same way every other web template does.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

* Bring Components.Gateway up to parity with Aspire BlazorGateway

Port the production-readiness pieces from Aspire's Gateway.cs.in into
Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Gateway so the framework-shipped gateway
behaves like the Aspire copy at runtime:

- ConfigureOpenTelemetry: OTel logging with formatted message + scopes,
  metrics for AspNetCore/HttpClient/Runtime, tracing with the app source
  + AspNetCore/HttpClient instrumentation, anti-feedback-loop filters
  for /_otlp/ requests and outbound /v1/* calls, and UseOtlpExporter()
  gated on OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT.
- Suppress per-request log noise from StaticAssets, Routing, and the
  OtlpExporter HttpClient.
- HSTS in non-development.
- Conditional HTTPS redirect only for document navigations
  (Sec-Fetch-Dest: document), so OTLP/API fetches are never redirected.
- /health and /alive health endpoints in development.
- ServiceDiscovery + StandardResilience on HttpClient defaults.

Skipped from Aspire's port because 11.0 makes them unnecessary:
- Per-app .Add(ep => reb.Order = int.MaxValue) hack — StaticAsset
  manifests now carry Order (#65975) and NegotiationMatcherPolicy
  respects routing priority (#65973), and the gateway already uses
  MapFallbackToFile for the SPA fallback.
- File-based-app properties (#:property ...) are net10.0-only.

Add OpenTelemetryInstrumentationAspNetCoreVersion to eng/Versions.props
and reference the OpenTelemetry + Http.Resilience packages directly from
the gateway csproj (it already opts into DisablePackageReferenceRestrictions).

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

* Move gateway dev-only log filters from code to RunArguments

The unconditional Microsoft.AspNetCore.StaticAssets / Routing and
System.Net.Http.HttpClient.OtlpExporter filters ported from Aspire's
Gateway.cs.in suppressed useful per-request logging in production.

Drop them from BlazorGateway.ConfigureOpenTelemetry and instead pass the
log-level overrides as --Logging:LogLevel:* command-line arguments from
Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Gateway.targets, alongside the existing
--environment Development argument. The args only take effect when the
gateway is launched via 'dotnet run' / IDE F5 through the package's
RunCommand, so production hosts (Aspire AppHost, direct
'dotnet blazor-gateway.dll' execution, integration tests) get the full
ASP.NET Core defaults.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

* Add BlazorGatewayOptions for configurable gateway behavior

Replace the hardcoded paths and feature toggles in BlazorGateway with a
typed options object bound from the BlazorGateway configuration section.
Source-generated configuration binding is implicit once PublishAot is
enabled on the gateway, so the call sites stay AOT-clean.

- Switch to WebApplication.CreateSlimBuilder for AOT readiness.
- Bind BlazorGatewayOptions from the 'BlazorGateway' section. Defaults
  live as property initializers on the options POCO.
- Gate every feature on the bound options:
  - Hsts.Enabled (only outside Development)
  - HttpsRedirection.Enabled (Sec-Fetch-Dest: document scope is fixed)
  - HealthChecks.Enabled + Path/LivenessPath/LivenessTag (only mapped
    in Development)
  - Telemetry.Enabled with configurable ExcludePaths /
    ExcludeOutboundPaths driving the AspNetCore + HttpClient
    instrumentation filters
  - HttpClient.ServiceDiscovery / StandardResilience
  - PathBase
- Drop the legacy lowercase 'pathbase' flat config key (replaced by
  BlazorGateway:PathBase). No backward-compatibility shim.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

* Add integration tests for Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Gateway

Replace the configuration-binding and telemetry-filter unit tests with
end-to-end coverage that boots BlazorGateway inside an in-process
TestServer and exercises each option through real HTTP traffic.

- Refactor BlazorGateway.BuildWebHost to expose an internal overload
  that accepts a pre-configured WebApplicationBuilder so tests can
  install UseTestServer before the gateway is built.
- Add explicit usings to BlazorGateway.cs so the file compiles outside
  Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web's GlobalUsings (the test project consumes the
  source via Compile Include and uses Microsoft.NET.Sdk).
- Drop BlazorGatewayOptionsTests and TelemetryFiltersTests in favor of
  the new BlazorGatewayTests scenarios.

Scenarios covered (14 tests, all passing):
  HealthChecks_ReturnsOk_InDevelopment_WithDefaultOptions
  HealthChecks_NotMapped_InProduction
  HealthChecks_Disabled_ReturnsNotFound_EvenInDevelopment
  HealthChecks_HonorsCustomPaths
  Hsts_HeaderEmitted_InProduction_WithDefaultOptions
  Hsts_HeaderAbsent_InDevelopment
  Hsts_Disabled_DoesNotEmitHeader_InProduction
  HttpsRedirection_RedirectsTopLevelNavigations_WithDefaultOptions
  HttpsRedirection_LeavesProgrammaticRequestsAlone
  HttpsRedirection_Disabled_DoesNotRedirectDocumentNavigations
  PathBase_MountsEndpointsUnderConfiguredPrefix
  ClientApps_ConfigEndpoint_ReturnsConfiguredJson

