* Remove inspectUri from Blazor template launchSettings.json

The inspectUri property steered F5 debugging through the legacy
DOTNET_MODIFIABLE_ASSEMBLIES Mono runtime debug proxy at
/_framework/debug/ws-proxy. The .NET 11 WASM debugger no longer
needs this hint, so drop it from the WASM and Blazor Web templates.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

* Fix Components.TestServer build break from BlazorGateway.cs changes

BlazorGateway.cs is compiled into Components.TestServer via a Compile
Include, but the new using directives (HealthChecks, OpenTelemetry)
introduced by this PR were not available to TestServer:

- Add <Reference> entries for Microsoft.AspNetCore.Diagnostics.HealthChecks
  and Microsoft.Extensions.Diagnostics.HealthChecks to TestServer.csproj.
- Add <Reference> entries for all OpenTelemetry and Http.Resilience packages
  used by BlazorGateway.cs.
- Also add Compile Include for BlazorGatewayOptions.cs and TelemetryFilters.cs
  which are now part of the gateway source.
- Register the new packages in eng/Dependencies.props as LatestPackageReference
  so they can be used via <Reference> in repo projects.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

* Add Microsoft.AspNetCore.HttpsPolicy to Components.TestServer

BlazorGateway.cs uses UseHsts() and UseHttpsRedirection() which are
defined in Microsoft.AspNetCore.HttpsPolicy. Components.TestServer
compiles BlazorGateway.cs directly via Compile Include but was
missing this reference, causing:

  CS1061: 'WebApplication' does not contain a definition for 'UseHsts'
  CS1061: 'IApplicationBuilder' does not contain a definition for 'UseHttpsRedirection'

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

* Make BlazorGateway liveness check shutdown-aware

Mirrors the AspNetCore.HealthChecks.ApplicationStatus behavior used by
the YARP container application (inline, no third-party dependency):
the 'self' check flips to Unhealthy as soon as IHostApplicationLifetime
signals ApplicationStopping, so Kubernetes/ACA stop routing new requests
to the pod during the drain window while in-flight requests complete.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

* Add BlazorGateway proxy and service-discovery test coverage

- Extract shared GatewayTestHelpers (StartGatewayAsync, StartUpstreamAsync)
  so tests can spin up a real Kestrel-hosted upstream alongside the
  TestServer-hosted gateway.
- Add BlazorGatewayProxyTests covering: no-config 404 fallback, request
  forwarding, path/query preservation, service-discovery resolution from
  configuration, and service-discovery disabled behavior.
- Only register the YARP service-discovery destination resolver when
  Gateway:HttpClient:ServiceDiscovery is enabled; otherwise YARP fails
  unrelated unresolved-service addresses at startup.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

* Remove BlazorGateway StandardResilience toggle

ConfigureHttpClientDefaults + AddStandardResilienceHandler only applies to
IHttpClientFactory clients. YARP's IForwarderHttpClientFactory builds an
HttpMessageInvoker directly around a SocketsHttpHandler and bypasses
IHttpClientFactory, so the toggle had no observable effect on proxied
traffic. The gateway has no other IHttpClientFactory consumers by default,
making the option dead code.

Remove the toggle, the registration, and the Microsoft.Extensions.Http.Resilience
package references from both src and test csproj files. Users who add their
own HttpClient consumers to the gateway can call AddStandardResilienceHandler
explicitly.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

* Make BlazorGateway service discovery unconditional; always map /alive

YARP container application treats service discovery as part of the contract
(always registers AddServiceDiscovery + AddServiceDiscoveryDestinationResolver
on the proxy). Match that:

- Remove the Gateway:HttpClient:ServiceDiscovery toggle and the now-empty
  HttpClientDefaultsOptions class.
- Always call AddServiceDiscovery() and AddServiceDiscoveryDestinationResolver().
- Drop the ConfigureHttpClientDefaults block (it only existed to add SD to all
  IHttpClientFactory clients, but the gateway has no such consumers OOB).

Also decouple the /alive liveness probe from /health: /alive is now mapped in
all environments (so external orchestrators can probe a running deployment)
while /health (the broader aggregate that can leak dependency status) remains
dev-only.

Tests updated:
- ServiceDiscovery_Disabled_LeavesUnresolvedAddress → ServiceDiscovery_UnresolvedAddress_FailsAtRequestTime.
- HealthChecks_NotMapped_InProduction → HealthChecks_Liveness_AlwaysMapped_Health_OnlyInDevelopment.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>

